FEATURE: cshapes-rectangle-fixes
DATE: 2026-10-11
SCOPE: bug fixes in CShapes fixedRectangle()/animatedRectangle(), plus config.radius

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AFFECTED PROJECTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

vUX: vUX-cShapes.js. Backwards compatible: the same config and methods, plus config.radius.
Square rectangles render as before (now sharp on retina); repeating animations with a dash period
that does not divide 100px move a few percent faster or slower so they loop without a jump.

vUX ProgressIndicator (grid type) uses animatedRectangle(): still paints and animates, checked.

Apps/vilshub.com: contact-form border uses radius 14; its stop-and-wait resize workaround and the
note about the numeric iterationCount bug are removed.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT CHANGED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Fixed: numeric iterationCount ReferenceError; path accumulation per frame; blurry canvas on
high-density screens; draw() during a run doubling the loop and stop() ignored on a cycle's last
frame; jump between cycles; easings not ending on 1 and duration 0 never completing; partial clear
with a non-zero origin; canvas id requirement.
Added: config.radius on both shapes; first frame painted synchronously in draw().

See logs/vUX-cShapes.js_ai_change.log for the verification run.
